==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Power Saw Cat '''at level 10.

Evolves into '''Neo Saw Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
In stages with enemies other than Aliens, Miter Saw Cat tends to be rather useless, with lower health than [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] and more than 6 times the recharge rate. Against Aliens, however, he proves to be pretty useful at his niche; his role is to be a tanker can both deal good damage and absorb numerous hits without having to worry about being teleported away by [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]].

In certain ways, Miter Saw Cat can be considered the [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] counterpart of [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], being a mini-tank and decent attacker against their targeted enemy trait. His 1,200¢ cost is also ideal for [[Cats of the Cosmos]], being able to bypass the restrictions imposed by many of the stages.

If you manage to get Miter Saw Cat during or before [[Into the Future]], he can carry you through most of the Alien-dominated stages, and helps greatly particularly in Chapter 1 Moon, where he can easily get in and damage [[Cli-One]].

Overall, Miter Saw Cat is a well-rounded anti-Alien unit whose impressive DPS, attack rate and health allows him to bulldoze through Aliens or majorly wear down a single target for a while. However, do note that his somewhat low damage per hit may mean that he won't be able to break tougher [[Barrier]]s. His deployment cooldown is also pretty lengthy, so be mindful on when to summon him.

He is quite a useful warp-immune tank, but it's quite a niche thing, as there are only two relevant units that are threats, [[Everlord Wanwan]] and [[Gardeneel Bros.]].

==='''True Form'''===
Neo Saw Cat's buffs are a straight improvement on what already made Power Saw great. His noticeable health increase, while not enough to give him good generalist usage, makes him significantly tankier against Aliens, and while his base damage increase may appear minimal, his rapid attack rate turns it into a major increase to his DPS. On top of that, his issues with Barriers have been fixed, as his new 20% chance to break them combined with his non-stop attacks makes him a very effective counter to tough Starred Aliens like [[UltraBaaBaa]], [[Youcan]] and [[Le'Solar]], his resistance and Immune to Warp allowing him to shatter them uninterrupted. Though the requirement of an [[Catfruit|Epic Catfruit Seed]] makes him unlikely to be available before [[Cats of the Cosmos]], where his strengths are most needed, it remains a worthwhile upgrade that enables him to compete with later Starred Aliens in [[Legend Stages]].

These allow Neo Saw Cat to become a very effective anti-Starred Alien tanker when highly leveled. A single Neo Saw Cat can even solo [[The Wormhole Opens (Deadly)|The Wormhole Opens]] with no problem whatsoever with all superior Cats of the Cosmos treasures obtained.

