==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 11.2 Update|Version 11.2]], Miter Saw Cat, [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]], [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Piledriver Cat]], [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cutter Cat]] and [[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Backhoe Cat]] could only be unlocked when "Grandon Mining Corps" was part of the current pool.
*Miter Saw Cat is the only Grandon Mining Corps unit whose Evolved Form's English name isn't just the Normal Form's with "Power" added in front, as it also drops the word "Miter".
*The second line of Miter Saw Cat's Japanese description, "He often cuts worthless objects," is a reference to [[wikipedia:Goemon Ishikawa XIII|Goemon Ishikawa XIII]]'s iconic catchphrase in ''[[wikipedia:Lupin the Third|Lupin III]]'', "I've cut yet another worthless object."
*The second line of Neo Saw Cat's Japanese description, "Synchro rate with the machine has increased to infinity," is a reference to the [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Synchronization synchronization rates] in ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'', particularly the scene in ''[https://wiki.evageeks.org/Evangelion:_3.0_%2B_1.0_Thrice_Upon_a_Time Evangelion: 3.0 + 1.0 Thrice Upon a Time]'' where [[Shinji & Cat (Rare Cat)|Shinji]]'s synchro rate with [[EVA Unit-01 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-01]] is revealed to have reached infinity.
*Miter Saw Cat could be seen in [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Guardians]]' attack animation before he was added to the game, albeit with a darker color scheme, two pilots instead of one, and the number "05" instead of "10".
**In the Ultra Form, [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Saviours]], a conceptual Ultra Form design for Miter Saw Cat, along with all other Grandon Mining Corps units can be seen during its attack animation. They have the same color scheme of all other [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] Ultra Forms, that being red and black with gold lining.

